From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:57:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui): synchronize adaptive sheet motion and selection
 actions

Share adaptive sheet state, geometry and lifecycle with Mihon 0088. Measure hidden anchor from actual sheet height; draw the scrim from visible fraction and disable duplicate native dim/animations. Animate back, outside and content dismissals before removing the dialog. Use native distance/velocity fling policy consistently for direct and nested content drags, retain list scrolling, block retiring actions and retain tablet presentation and fork width adapters. Interpolate natural pager heights during held swipes in both directions. Remove the library action bar extra 300ms delay and use common compact button/padding metrics for book and chapter selection; retain confirmation and gesture insets. Cover remaining bare native LazyColumn/LazyRow calls with existing frame-time protection and align standalone tracker/settings search headers, retaining purpose-built player headers. Add seven Compose lifecycle, content distance/velocity, held-swipe height and immediate selection bar regressions. Device visual behavior remains pending user installation; existing fling clock kernel and capsule shaders are unchanged.
